  "articleBody": "When you're dealing with storm-damaged drywall, it's easy to make a few missteps that can cause bigger headaches down the road. One of the biggest mistakes is cutting too small of a repair opening. You might think you’re minimizing the work, but it can lead to missing hidden wet insulation or moisture, which is a recipe for mold. Another common error is skipping mold checks; always be vigilant for signs of mold, even if it's just a musty odor. And this is a super important one: make absolutely sure the source of the water intrusion is completely stopped before you even think about starting repairs. Otherwise, you'll be fixing the same problem again. For really extensive damage, or if you suspect structural issues, getting a professional opinion can save you a ton of time and money in the long run. HH Remodeling LLC has seen it all and can help you avoid these pitfalls, ensuring your storm-related drywall replacement is done right the first time.",
